description: Git permission — no pull/push/commit unless user explicitly asks
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git

- **Never** `git pull`, `git push`, or `git commit` (including amend, `--no-verify`, or hooks that commit) unless the user **explicitly asks in this conversation**.
- Allowed without asking: read-only git (`status`, `diff`, `log`, `show`).
- If commit/push/pull would help, ask first and wait.
- Do not update git config.
